I have read through many of the Windows users who have had Rattle installation problems. I have tried all of the fixes that I found and that seemed to apply to my problems. I have updated all required packages and I have followed, or tried to follow, the internet-connected installation instructions. The results of rattle.info <http://rattle.info>() are shown below.

For some reason every time I attempt to launch Rattle with rattle() I am prompted with the Need GTK+?... dialogue box. I have been through so many uninstalls and reinstalls that I have honestly lost count. Once I get through another reinstall I get the same error when trying to launch rattle():

